From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: feature/round-video-lenses: back camera lens button for video messages via CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO

RoundVideoCameraController gets a base zoom ratio for the back camera (the selected lens,
below 1 = ultra-wide of a logical multi-camera); pinch zoom multiplies it and the result is
clamped to CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO_RANGE, or to at least 1 on the crop-region path. The initial
value is the start lens chosen in Neogram settings. isPreferredCameraCandidate lets
NeoRoundCamera pick the back camera the lens catalog describes when it reaches an
ultra-wide; otherwise the stock choice stays. RoundVideoSession.neo_setBaseZoomRatio stores
the ratio and applies it right away only while recording and not switching cameras, like
setZoom. InstantCameraView2 adds NeoLensButton after the flash button and feeds it the
camera capabilities, the session start and the camera-control state.
